@startuml seq_ai_tutor_chatbot
!theme plain
skinparam defaultFontName Arial
skinparam defaultFontSize 11
skinparam SequenceArrowThickness 1.5

title Sequence: AI Tutor Chatbot\n(Context Token -> Hybrid RAG -> SSE)

actor "Learner" as Learner
participant "web-bff\n(Next.js)" as Web
participant "core-api" as Core
participant "chat-service" as Chat
participant "BGE-M3\nEmbedder" as Embedder
database "Qdrant\nlearning_chunks" as Qdrant
database "Neo4j\nKnowledge Graph" as Neo4j
participant "RRF + Graph-aware\nReranker" as Reranker
participant "LLM\nGemini" as LLM
database "PostgreSQL" as PG

== Context authorization ==
Learner -> Web : type question
Web -> Core : POST /chat/context-token\nsession + course context
Core -> Core : validate LTI session\nrole + course access
Core --> Web : short-lived JWT\nallowed course / document / LO ids

== SSE chat stream ==
Web -> Chat : GET /chat/stream\nJWT ticket + question
Chat -> Chat : validate JWT\nscope + expiry
Chat -> Embedder : embed dense + sparse(question)
Embedder --> Chat : dense vector\n+ sparse weights

== Hybrid retrieval ==
Chat -> Qdrant : dense search\nfilter={course_id, allowed_lo_ids}
Qdrant --> Chat : dense_results[]
Chat -> Qdrant : sparse search\nfilter={course_id, allowed_lo_ids}
Qdrant --> Chat : sparse_results[]
Chat -> Reranker : RRF fusion\n(dense, sparse)
Reranker --> Chat : fused_candidates[]

== Graph-aware context ==
Chat -> Neo4j : MATCH chunk -> LO / Chapter / Concept\nwithin allowed scope
Neo4j --> Chat : graph_context\nLO paths + prerequisite links
Chat -> Reranker : boost_by_graph_context\n(fused_candidates, graph_context)
Reranker --> Chat : final_context\nwith citations

== Answer streaming ==
Chat -> LLM : generate_stream\nquestion + final_context + guardrails
LLM --> Chat : token stream
Chat --> Web : SSE token\nanswer fragment + citation refs
Web --> Learner : render realtime answer
LLM --> Chat : done
Chat --> Web : event=done\ncitation list
Web --> Learner : show source references

== Audit ==
Chat -> PG : INSERT chat_messages\nquestion, answer, chunks_used

@enduml
